  "details": "A while back in the comments of this canny post I discovered weird behavior with animators on the IKpose layer using the 'TrackingType' parameter:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-ik-20/p/knee-bend-prediction-in-202212p4-in-fullbody-causes-specific-avatars-knees-to-bu\n\nSpecifically, I make use of an animator on the IK pose layer to check which tracking type I'm using (3pt or 6pt) to correct the bend angle of the legs of the avatar I use. This uses the 'TrackingType' parameter. \n\nIn the current live build of the game, it seems the IK Pose layer only updates properly on avatar load. Meaning in order to have it properly update the current state, I need to reset the avatar. I would have to do this for every world change.\n\nHowever, in the current beta, the ikpose layer seems to just never move past the first state. I'm unsure if this is a bug with the layer, or if this is a bug with the TrackingType parameter. Or if this is an optimization and the ikpose layer is never meant to have any states in it on purpose.\n\n\nExample avatar: avtr_b5022a87-8a38-49e1-a22e-1a5d356d85b9\n\nInstructions (Using 6pt tracking and height measurement mode): \n\nIn live build: If knees bend forwards, the state is in '3pt' and you need to hit reset avatar to make it update to 6pt\n\nIn beta build: The layer (Or parameter) never seems to update.\n\nBeyond this, I'm unsure how I could debug it any further. The IKpose layer seems to only work if something is in the default state.",
